    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c2a06be_2ec28f70",
        "filename": "chip/g/nvmem_utils.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000058
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-03-23T21:46:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re inconsistent between sizes and signedness in block indices. phy_block and cache_block are int16, yet are assigned to and from int, int8_t, uint32_t. I\u0027d suggest either int or uint32_t everywhere.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "5760325b7541a45a59f8619b95389f35b9f395a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9c2a06be_3a412984",
        "filename": "chip/g/nvmem_utils.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 131,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-03-24T18:29:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I want the indices to be signed so that -1 can be used to mark table entry as non-initialized. So I am making sure that the table entries for indices are ints. W.R.T to the tags, the block index will remain a int8_t as I don\u0027t want to make the tag space larger than necessary. The version entry is only one that I will keep as signed since conceptually I think it\u0027s better for the version to span 0 -\u003e 0xFE.",
      "parentUuid": "9c2a06be_2ec28f70",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 130,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "5760325b7541a45a59f8619b95389f35b9f395a4",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
