    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9cb1265a_f112c898",
        "filename": "chip/g/nvmem_utils.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 300,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-03-24T18:29:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "nvmem_resovle_dup() just looks at 2 phy blocks which have the same logical block number in the tag and returns the most recent of the two by comparing the version numbers. The function verify_log_to_phy_map() would catch the case where more than two phy blocks contain the same log block number.\n\nHowever, two phy blocks (in flash) having the same logical block and version number, the resolve_dup function would by default use the 1st of those phy blocks encountered.",
      "parentUuid": "9c2a06be_79fa9388",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 300,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 300,
        "endChar": 21
      },
